<title>JAPAN: Taisei -6mth parent results.</title>
<headline>Taisei -6mth parent results.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p> (Parent)	(in billions of yen unless specified)</p>
<p> Sales		  6.55		vs	    6.42</p>
<p> Operating	  301    million	  vs	  349    million</p>
<p> Current	    360    million	  vs	  497    million</p>
<p> Net		  211    million	  vs	  263    million</p>
<p> EPS		   51.94 yen	  vs	   66.05 yen</p>
<p> Shares		5 million	  vs	 333,000</p>
<p> Interim div	  0.00 yen	  vs	    0.00 yen</p>
<p>NOTE - Taisei Co Ltd is a service company, involved</p>
<p>mostly in building maintenance.</p>
<p>It changed its shares' face value to 50 yen from 500</p>
<p>yen on July 30, 1996. Also it implemented a 1:1.2 share</p>
<p>split on the same day. Taisei's EPS for the 1995/96 first</p>
<p>half above was base on the same conditions as it</p>
<p>calculated the EPS for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
</text>
